  "notes": "The club-and-oddball corner of the Atlanta bench, and its identity is the research's phrase \"the deliberate anti-trap drum layer\". The kick is a steady quarter-note pulse — `densityPerBar` fixed at 4, `anchors` on all four beats, `syncopation` 0.08, which is by far the lowest number in this batch — while the clap still lands on 3, so `halfTime` stays inherited and the two readings the research gives (slow 4/4 club, half-time trap) are the same grid. Hats are straight and roll almost never (`hihat.fill.prob` 0.12), open hats are raised to 0.35 for the house lineage, and the sub is a clean drone with no distortion and slow glides. Melody is long notes at low density over 4- and 8-bar pad loops, which is why `phraseBars` reaches 8 — the only entry here that does. ⚠ `bassline.rhythm` is `mirror_kick`, and that is an engine limit rather than a reading of the record: the research describes a sustained sub drone, and with a four-on-the-floor kick above it `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.95 restates the same root every beat rather than holding it. It is the nearest honest thing the generator can produce; `glideProb` 0.5 carries the slow glides. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and marks the internals [LOW-CONF] — `lockTo808` 0.4, the hat numbers and the pad register are the inferred parameters. The two-chord families are what the research names (\"two-chord loops\" over \"a dance-music tonic pedal\").",
